 g:{
 topic:["Possessives: my, his, her and 's","الملكية: my و his و her و 's"], level:"A1–A2",
 obj:[["Say who things and people belong to.","التعبير عن ملكية الأشياء وصلة القرابة."],["Use my, your, his, her, its, our and their correctly.","استخدام my و your و his و her و its و our و their بشكل صحيح."],["Add 's to a name or a noun.","إضافة 's إلى اسم علم أو اسم."]],
 en:["Possessive adjectives come before a noun and show who it belongs to: my, your, his, her, its, our, their. They never change: \"my son\", \"my sons\".","Choose his or her by looking at the owner, not at the thing. A man's wife is \"his wife\"; a woman's husband is \"her husband\".","With a name or a noun, add 's: \"my wife's name\", \"Ali's brother\". The owner comes first. For a plural that ends in -s, add only the apostrophe: \"my parents' house\".","To ask about the owner, use Whose: \"Whose car is this?\" The answer can be short: \"It's my brother's.\""],
 ar:["صفات الملكية تأتي قبل الاسم وتبيّن صاحبه: my و your و his و her و its و our و their. وهي لا تتغير أبدًا: my son و my sons.","نختار his أو her بحسب المالك وليس بحسب الشيء المملوك. زوجة الرجل his wife، وزوج المرأة her husband.","مع اسم العلم أو الاسم نضيف 's: my wife's name و Ali's brother. والمالك يأتي أولًا، بعكس ترتيب الإضافة في العربية. ومع الجمع المنتهي بـ s نضيف الفاصلة العليا فقط: my parents' house.","للسؤال عن المالك نستخدم Whose: Whose car is this? والإجابة قد تكون قصيرة: It's my brother's."],
 forms:[
 ["Affirmative","الإثبات","my / his / her / our / their + noun  ·  noun + 's + noun","Their house has a big garden.","My wife's name is Dina."],
 ["Negative","النفي","It isn't + possessive + noun","It isn't my car.","That isn't my brother's house."],
 ["Question","السؤال","Whose + noun + is this?  ·  Is this your + noun?","Whose car is this?","Is that your nephew?"]
 ],
