 g:{
 topic:["There is / There are","There is / There are"], level:"A1–A2",
 obj:[["Say what exists in a place.","ذكر ما يوجد في مكان ما."],["Choose is or are from the noun that follows.","اختيار is أو are بحسب الاسم التالي."],["Ask and answer with Is there…? and Are there any…?","السؤال والإجابة باستخدام Is there و Are there any."]],
 en:["We use There is and There are to say that something exists or is in a place. They are how English says the Arabic «يوجد» or «في»: \"There's a park near my house.\"","Use There is (There's) before a singular noun and There are before a plural noun. When you list things, the verb follows the first one: \"There's an oven and two fridges.\"","In the negative, say There isn't a… for one thing and There aren't any… for many. In questions, put the verb first: Is there a balcony? Are there any shops?","Use There is the first time you mention something. After that, use It is or They are to describe it: \"There's a park nearby. It's very big.\""],
 ar:["نستخدم There is و There are لنقول إن شيئًا موجود في مكان ما. وهما مقابل «يوجد» أو «في» بالعربية: There's a park near my house.","نستخدم There is (واختصارها There's) قبل الاسم المفرد، و There are قبل الجمع. وعند ذكر قائمة يتبع الفعل أول عنصر فيها: There's an oven and two fridges.","في النفي نقول There isn't a… للمفرد و There aren't any… للجمع. وفي السؤال نقدّم الفعل: Is there a balcony? Are there any shops?","نستخدم There is عند ذكر الشيء لأول مرة. وبعد ذلك نستخدم It is أو They are لوصفه: There's a park nearby. It's very big."],
 forms:[
 ["Affirmative","الإثبات","There is (There's) + a / an + singular  ·  There are + plural","There's a lamp on the desk.","There are four chairs around the table."],
 ["Negative","النفي","There isn't + a / an + singular  ·  There aren't any + plural","There isn't a garden, but there's a park nearby.","There aren't any pictures on the walls yet."],
 ["Question","السؤال","Is there + a / an…?  ·  Are there any…?","Is there an elevator in the building?","Are there any shops near your building?"]
 ],
