 obj:[["Tell countable nouns from uncountable nouns.","التمييز بين الأسماء المعدودة وغير المعدودة."],["Use some and any correctly.","استخدام some و any بشكل صحيح."],["Ask about quantity and price with How much and How many.","السؤال عن الكمية والسعر بـ How much و How many."]],
 en:["English nouns are countable (an egg, two eggs) or uncountable (milk, rice, sugar). Uncountable nouns have no plural and do not take a or an: we say \"some rice\", not \"a rice\" or \"rices\".","Use some in positive sentences, and any in negatives and most questions: \"We have some chicken\", \"We don't have any fish\", \"Do you have any eggs?\" In offers and requests, some is normal: \"Can I have some cheese?\"","Use How many with countable nouns and How much with uncountable nouns. How much also asks about the price: \"How much is this chicken?\"","To count an uncountable noun, use a container or a measure: a bottle of oil, a kilo of rice, a loaf of bread."],
 ar:["الأسماء في الإنجليزية إما معدودة (an egg, two eggs) أو غير معدودة (milk, rice, sugar). وغير المعدودة لا تُجمع ولا تأخذ a أو an: نقول some rice وليس a rice أو rices.","نستخدم some في الإثبات، و any في النفي ومعظم الأسئلة: We have some chicken، We don't have any fish، Do you have any eggs? وفي العرض والطلب نستخدم some: Can I have some cheese?","نستخدم How many مع المعدود و How much مع غير المعدود. وتُستخدم How much أيضًا للسؤال عن السعر: How much is this chicken?","لعدّ الاسم غير المعدود نستخدم وعاءً أو وحدة قياس: a bottle of oil، a kilo of rice، a loaf of bread."],
