 en:["We use a comparative to compare two things. The word than comes after it: \"The blue shirt is cheaper than the white one.\"","Short adjectives take -er: cheap → cheaper, warm → warmer. If the adjective ends in one vowel + one consonant, double the consonant: big → bigger. If it ends in -y, change y to i: busy → busier, easy → easier.","Long adjectives, with two or more syllables, take more: more expensive, more comfortable, more formal. Never use more and -er together.","A few are irregular: good → better, bad → worse, far → farther. To say two things are not equal, you can also use not as … as: \"The gray jacket isn't as warm as the black one.\""],
 ar:["نستخدم صيغة المقارنة للمقارنة بين شيئين. وتأتي بعدها كلمة than: The blue shirt is cheaper than the white one.","الصفات القصيرة تأخذ er: cheap ← cheaper و warm ← warmer. وإذا انتهت الصفة بحرف علّة واحد ثم حرف ساكن واحد نضاعف الحرف الأخير: big ← bigger. وإذا انتهت بـ y نحوّلها إلى i: busy ← busier و easy ← easier.","الصفات الطويلة، من مقطعين أو أكثر، تأخذ more: more expensive و more comfortable و more formal. ولا نجمع أبدًا بين more و er.","بعض الصفات شاذة: good ← better و bad ← worse و far ← farther. ولنفي التساوي يمكن أيضًا استخدام not as … as: The gray jacket isn't as warm as the black one."],
