 obj:[["Describe the number one in a group with the -est and the most.","وصف الأول في مجموعته باستخدام the -est و the most."],["Use the irregular forms best and worst.","استخدام الصيغ الشاذة best و worst."],["Recommend places and options.","ترشيح الأماكن والخيارات."]],
 en:["We use a superlative to compare one thing with all the others in a group: \"Cairo is the biggest city in Egypt.\" It always takes the.","Short adjectives take -est: cheap → the cheapest, old → the oldest. The spelling rules are the same as for comparatives: big → the biggest, busy → the busiest.","Long adjectives take the most: the most famous, the most beautiful, the most interesting. Never use most and -est together.","Irregular forms: good → the best, bad → the worst, far → the farthest. After a superlative, use in with places and groups (\"in Egypt\", \"in town\", \"in the team\") and of with periods of time (\"of the year\", \"of the day\")."],
 ar:["نستخدم صيغة التفضيل لمقارنة شيء واحد بكل ما في مجموعته: Cairo is the biggest city in Egypt. وهي تأخذ the دائمًا.","الصفات القصيرة تأخذ est: cheap ← the cheapest و old ← the oldest. وقواعد الإملاء هي نفسها في صيغة المقارنة: big ← the biggest و busy ← the busiest.","الصفات الطويلة تأخذ the most: the most famous و the most beautiful و the most interesting. ولا نجمع أبدًا بين most و est.","الصيغ الشاذة: good ← the best و bad ← the worst و far ← the farthest. وبعد صيغة التفضيل نستخدم in مع الأماكن والمجموعات (in Egypt و in town و in the team) و of مع الفترات الزمنية (of the year و of the day)."],
 forms:[
