 en:["We use the imperative to give directions, instructions and advice. It is simply the base form of the verb, with no subject: \"Turn left\", \"Take the metro\".","For the negative, put Don't before the verb: \"Don't turn right at the square.\"","An imperative can sound strong. To be polite, add please, or use Could you…? when you ask someone to do something for you: \"Please stop here\", \"Could you tell me the way?\"","Directions need the small words of place and movement: at the lights, on the right, next to, opposite, behind, between, past, across, through, up and down."],
 ar:["نستخدم صيغة الأمر لإعطاء الاتجاهات والتعليمات والنصائح. وهي ببساطة الفعل في صورته الأصلية بدون فاعل: Turn left، Take the metro.","للنفي نضع Don't قبل الفعل: Don't turn right at the square.","صيغة الأمر قد تبدو حادّة. ولتكون مهذبًا أضف please، أو استخدم Could you…? عندما تطلب من شخص أن يفعل شيئًا لك: Please stop here، Could you tell me the way?","الاتجاهات تحتاج كلمات المكان والحركة القصيرة: at the lights و on the right و next to و opposite و behind و between و past و across و through و up و down."],
