 obj:[["Give advice with should and shouldn't.","تقديم النصيحة باستخدام should و shouldn't."],["Ask for advice with Should I…?","طلب النصيحة باستخدام Should I…?"],["Use the base verb after should.","استخدام الفعل في صورته الأصلية بعد should."]],
 en:["We use should to give advice or to say that something is a good idea: \"You should see a doctor.\" We use shouldn't when something is a bad idea: \"You shouldn't go to work tomorrow.\"","Should is a modal verb. It is the same for every subject and never takes -s. The verb after it is the base form, without to: \"He should rest\", not \"He shoulds rest\" or \"He should to rest\".","To ask for advice, put should before the subject: \"Should I stay in bed?\", \"What should I eat?\"","Should is softer than must and have to. It gives an opinion, not a rule. To sound even softer, start with I think: \"I think you should talk to your manager.\""],
 ar:["نستخدم should لتقديم النصيحة أو لنقول إن شيئًا ما فكرة جيدة: You should see a doctor. ونستخدم shouldn't عندما يكون الشيء فكرة سيئة: You shouldn't go to work tomorrow.","should فعل ناقص. لا يتغير مع أي فاعل ولا يأخذ s أبدًا. والفعل بعده يكون في صورته الأصلية بدون to: نقول He should rest وليس He shoulds rest أو He should to rest.","لطلب النصيحة نقدّم should على الفاعل: Should I stay in bed? و What should I eat?","should ألطف من must و have to. فهي رأي وليست قاعدة ملزمة. ولتكون ألطف أكثر ابدأ بـ I think: I think you should talk to your manager."],
