 obj:[["Talk about where you were and how things were.","التحدث عن مكانك في الماضي وكيف كانت الأشياء."],["Use was and were with the right subject.","استخدام was و were مع الفاعل المناسب."],["Make negatives and questions in the past of to be.","تكوين النفي والسؤال في ماضي فعل to be."]],
 en:["Was and were are the past forms of am, is and are. We use them to describe people, places and situations in the past: \"The weather was cold\", \"We were late\".","Use was with I, he, she and it. Use were with you, we and they. A common slip is \"you was\"; it is always \"you were\".","For the negative, add not: wasn't, weren't. For a question, put was or were first: \"Was the meeting useful?\", \"Where were you?\" We never use did with was and were.","There was and There were are the past of There is and There are. To say when and where your life began, use was born: \"I was born in Giza.\""],
 ar:["was و were هما ماضي am و is و are. نستخدمهما لوصف الأشخاص والأماكن والمواقف في الماضي: The weather was cold و We were late.","نستخدم was مع I و he و she و it. ونستخدم were مع you و we و they. ومن الأخطاء الشائعة you was، والصحيح دائمًا you were.","للنفي نضيف not: wasn't و weren't. وللسؤال نقدّم was أو were: Was the meeting useful? و Where were you? ولا نستخدم did أبدًا مع was و were.","There was و There were هما ماضي There is و There are. ولتذكر متى وأين وُلدت استخدم was born: I was born in Giza."],
