 obj:[["Use the past forms of the most common irregular verbs.","استخدام ماضي أكثر الأفعال الشاذة شيوعًا."],["Tell the story of a trip.","حكاية رحلة."],["Notice the patterns that make the forms easier to remember.","ملاحظة الأنماط التي تسهّل حفظ الصيغ."]],
 en:["Many of the most common English verbs are irregular: they do not take -ed in the past. You have to learn each past form: go → went, have → had, see → saw.","Like regular verbs, the past form is the same for every subject: I went, she went, they went.","Some patterns help you remember. The vowel changes: come → came, swim → swam, meet → met. The ending changes to -t or -ght: leave → left, send → sent, spend → spent, buy → bought. A few change completely: go → went.","The irregular form is used only in positive sentences. After didn't and Did, the verb goes back to its base form: \"I didn't go\", \"Did you see it?\" You will practise this on Day 16."],
 ar:["كثير من أكثر الأفعال الإنجليزية شيوعًا أفعال شاذة: لا تأخذ ed في الماضي. ولا بد من حفظ كل صيغة: go ← went و have ← had و see ← saw.","ومثل الأفعال المنتظمة، صيغة الماضي واحدة مع كل الفاعلين: I went و she went و they went.","بعض الأنماط تساعدك على الحفظ. حرف العلّة يتغير: come ← came و swim ← swam و meet ← met. أو تتحول النهاية إلى t أو ght: leave ← left و send ← sent و spend ← spent و buy ← bought. وقليل منها يتغير تمامًا: go ← went.","الصيغة الشاذة تُستخدم في الإثبات فقط. وبعد didn't و Did يرجع الفعل إلى صورته الأصلية: I didn't go و Did you see it? وستتدرب على ذلك في اليوم 16."],
 forms:[
 ["Affirmative","الإثبات","Subject + irregular past form","Last month we went to Alexandria by train.","I bought some gifts for my parents."],
 ["Negative","النفي","Subject + didn't + base verb (practised on Day 16)","We didn't go by car.","I didn't buy anything."],
 ["Question","السؤال","Did + subject + base verb ? (practised on Day 16)","Did you see the library?","Did they come back on Sunday?"]
 ],
