 obj:[["Talk about plans you have already decided.","التحدث عن خطط قرّرتها بالفعل."],["Make predictions from what you can see now.","التوقّع بناءً على ما تراه الآن."],["Form negatives and questions with be going to.","تكوين النفي والسؤال باستخدام be going to."]],
 en:["We use be going to for plans and intentions: things we have already decided to do. \"I'm going to book the tickets tonight\" means the decision is made.","The form is am, is or are + going to + base verb. Only the verb to be changes: I'm going to pack, she's going to choose, they're going to learn.","For the negative, add not after am, is or are: \"I'm not going to check my email.\" For a question, put am, is or are first: \"Are you going to rent a car?\"","We also use it to predict something when we can see the evidence now: \"Look at those clouds. It's going to rain.\" In fast speech, going to often sounds like \"gonna\". Understand it when you hear it, but write going to."],
 ar:["نستخدم be going to للخطط والنوايا: أشياء قرّرنا فعلها بالفعل. جملة I'm going to book the tickets tonight تعني أن القرار قد اتُّخذ.","التركيب: am أو is أو are + going to + الفعل في صورته الأصلية. والذي يتغير هو فعل to be فقط: I'm going to pack و she's going to choose و they're going to learn.","للنفي نضيف not بعد am أو is أو are: I'm not going to check my email. وللسؤال نقدّمها: Are you going to rent a car?","ونستخدمها أيضًا للتوقّع عندما نرى الدليل الآن: Look at those clouds. It's going to rain. وفي الكلام السريع تُسمع going to مثل «جَنَ» (gonna). افهمها عندما تسمعها، لكن اكتب going to."],
 forms:[
 ["Affirmative","الإثبات","Subject + am / is / are + going to + base verb","I'm going to book the tickets tonight.","The kids are going to learn to dive."],
 ["Negative","النفي","Subject + am not / isn't / aren't + going to + base verb","I'm not going to check my email on holiday.","We aren't going to take much luggage."],
 ["Question","السؤال","Am / Is / Are + subject + going to + base verb ?","Are you going to rent a car?","What are you going to do there?"]
