 obj:[["Make promises and offers with I'll.","تقديم الوعود والعروض باستخدام I'll."],["Say what you decide at the moment of speaking.","التعبير عن قرار تتخذه لحظة الكلام."],["Predict what you think will happen.","توقّع ما تظن أنه سيحدث."]],
 en:["We use will when we decide something at the moment of speaking: \"The phone is ringing. I'll get it.\" We also use it to promise and to offer help: \"I'll send you the report by noon\", \"I'll help you with those boxes\".","Will is a modal verb. It is the same for every subject, and the verb after it is the base form: \"She will approve it\", never \"She wills\" or \"will to approve\". In speaking, use the short form 'll.","The negative is won't (will not): \"I won't forget.\" For a question, put will first: \"Will you be in the office tomorrow?\" Short answers use the full form: \"Yes, I will\", \"No, I won't\".","Use will for predictions that are your opinion, often with I think, I'm sure or probably: \"I think the project will finish on time.\" For plans you have already made, use be going to instead."],
 ar:["نستخدم will عندما نقرّر شيئًا لحظة الكلام: The phone is ringing. I'll get it. ونستخدمها أيضًا للوعد ولعرض المساعدة: I'll send you the report by noon و I'll help you with those boxes.","will فعل ناقص. لا يتغير مع أي فاعل، والفعل بعده يكون في صورته الأصلية: She will approve it وليس She wills أو will to approve. وفي الكلام نستخدم الاختصار 'll.","النفي هو won't (will not): I won't forget. وللسؤال نقدّم will: Will you be in the office tomorrow? والإجابات القصيرة تكون بالصيغة الكاملة: Yes, I will و No, I won't.","نستخدم will للتوقعات التي تعبّر عن رأيك، وغالبًا مع I think أو I'm sure أو probably: I think the project will finish on time. أما الخطط التي قرّرتها مسبقًا فنستخدم معها be going to."],
