 en:["We use must for rules and strong obligations: \"You must wear your ID card.\" Have to means almost the same and is more common in everyday speech: \"You have to finish the training this month.\"","Must is a modal verb: no -s, no to after it, the same form for every subject. \"She must sign in\", not \"She musts\" or \"must to sign\".","The two negatives mean very different things. Mustn't means it is forbidden: \"You mustn't share your password.\" Don't have to means it is not necessary, but you can if you want: \"You don't have to wear a tie on Thursdays.\"","Questions are usually made with have to: \"Do I have to ask for permission?\" For the past, both use had to: \"Yesterday I had to stay late.\""],
 ar:["نستخدم must للقواعد والالتزامات القوية: You must wear your ID card. و have to لها المعنى نفسه تقريبًا، وهي أكثر شيوعًا في الكلام اليومي: You have to finish the training this month.","must فعل ناقص: لا يأخذ s، ولا تأتي بعده to، وصيغته واحدة مع كل الفاعلين. نقول She must sign in وليس She musts أو must to sign.","صيغتا النفي معناهما مختلف تمامًا. mustn't تعني أن الشيء ممنوع: You mustn't share your password. أما don't have to فتعني أنه غير ضروري، لكنك تستطيع فعله إن أردت: You don't have to wear a tie on Thursdays.","الأسئلة تُصاغ غالبًا بـ have to: Do I have to ask for permission? وفي الماضي تتحول الاثنتان إلى had to: Yesterday I had to stay late."],
