 topic:["Object Pronouns","ضمائر المفعول"], level:"A2",
 obj:[["Use me, you, him, her, it, us and them after verbs and prepositions.","استخدام me و you و him و her و it و us و them بعد الأفعال وحروف الجر."],["Put two objects in the right order.","ترتيب مفعولين ترتيبًا صحيحًا."],["Handle a phone call politely.","إدارة مكالمة هاتفية بأدب."]],
 en:["Subject pronouns (I, you, he, she, it, we, they) come before the verb. Object pronouns (me, you, him, her, it, us, them) come after the verb or after a preposition: \"She called me\", \"I spoke to her\".","You and it do not change. The others do: I → me, he → him, she → her, we → us, they → them.","Some verbs take two objects, such as give, send, tell and email. There are two correct orders: \"I sent him the contract\" or \"I sent the contract to him\". When the thing is it or them, use only the second order: \"I sent it to him\", not \"I sent him it\".","In natural speech these little words are weak and join the verb: \"tell him\" sounds like \"tellim\" and \"ask her\" sounds like \"asker\"."],
 ar:["ضمائر الفاعل (I و you و he و she و it و we و they) تأتي قبل الفعل. وضمائر المفعول (me و you و him و her و it و us و them) تأتي بعد الفعل أو بعد حرف الجر: She called me و I spoke to her.","you و it لا يتغيران. والبقية تتغير: I ← me و he ← him و she ← her و we ← us و they ← them.","بعض الأفعال تأخذ مفعولين، مثل give و send و tell و email. وهناك ترتيبان صحيحان: I sent him the contract أو I sent the contract to him. وإذا كان الشيء it أو them فنستخدم الترتيب الثاني فقط: I sent it to him وليس I sent him it.","في الكلام الطبيعي تُنطق هذه الكلمات الصغيرة خفيفة وتلتصق بالفعل: tell him تُسمع «تِلِم» و ask her تُسمع «آسكَر»."],
