 en:["Short, separate sentences sound like a list. Linking words join them into a story. And adds an idea, but shows a contrast, so gives a result, and because gives a reason: \"I was worried, so I called a friend.\"","Because and so are two sides of the same idea. \"I stayed home because I was sick\" and \"I was sick, so I stayed home\" mean the same. Never use both in one sentence.","To put events in order, use first, then, after that and finally. When and before join two actions in time: \"When I arrived, the manager welcomed me.\"","Although and however also show contrast. Although joins two parts of one sentence and is not used with but: \"Although I was tired, I didn't give up.\" However starts a new sentence and is followed by a comma: \"I was nervous. However, I practiced a lot.\""],
 ar:["الجمل القصيرة المنفصلة تبدو كقائمة. وأدوات الربط تحوّلها إلى حكاية. and تضيف فكرة، و but تبيّن التضاد، و so تذكر النتيجة، و because تذكر السبب: I was worried, so I called a friend.","because و so وجهان لفكرة واحدة. جملة I stayed home because I was sick وجملة I was sick, so I stayed home لهما المعنى نفسه. ولا نجمع بينهما أبدًا في جملة واحدة.","لترتيب الأحداث نستخدم first و then و after that و finally. و when و before تربطان فعلين في الزمن: When I arrived, the manager welcomed me.","although و however تدلّان على التضاد أيضًا. although تربط جزأين في جملة واحدة ولا تأتي معها but: Although I was tired, I didn't give up. أما however فتبدأ جملة جديدة وتتبعها فاصلة: I was nervous. However, I practiced a lot."],
 forms:[
