 obj:[["Join two verbs correctly.","ربط فعلين متتاليين ربطًا صحيحًا."],["Remember which verbs take to and which take -ing.","حفظ الأفعال التي يأتي بعدها to والتي يأتي بعدها ing."],["Talk about goals, plans and habits.","التحدث عن الأهداف والخطط والعادات."]],
 en:["When two verbs come together, the second one is either to + verb or verb + -ing. The first verb decides which one.","These verbs are followed by to + verb: want, need, hope, plan, decide, learn, promise, try, manage, intend and would like. \"I want to improve\", \"I've decided to study\".","These verbs are followed by -ing: enjoy, finish, keep, stop, avoid, mind, practice and can't stand. \"I enjoy listening\", \"I keep making mistakes\". A verb after a preposition is also -ing: \"I look forward to hearing from you\".","Like, love, hate and start can take both forms. To make the second verb negative, put not before it: \"I decided not to wait.\" With want and would like you can name the person who should act: \"My manager wants me to lead a project\", never \"wants that I lead\"."],
 ar:["عندما يأتي فعلان متتاليان يكون الثاني إما to + فعل أو فعل + ing. والفعل الأول هو الذي يحدد ذلك.","هذه الأفعال يأتي بعدها to + فعل: want و need و hope و plan و decide و learn و promise و try و manage و intend و would like. مثل: I want to improve و I've decided to study.","وهذه الأفعال يأتي بعدها ing: enjoy و finish و keep و stop و avoid و mind و practice و can't stand. مثل: I enjoy listening و I keep making mistakes. والفعل بعد حرف الجر يأخذ ing أيضًا: I look forward to hearing from you.","like و love و hate و start تقبل الصيغتين. ولنفي الفعل الثاني نضع not قبله: I decided not to wait. ومع want و would like يمكن ذكر الشخص المطلوب منه الفعل: My manager wants me to lead a project، ولا نقول أبدًا wants that I lead."],
