how:"في كل كلمة إنجليزية مقطع واحد مشدَّد يُنطق أطول وأعلى وأوضح. وإضافة ‎-ly‎ لا تغيّر مكان النبر: CAREful تصير CAREfully، و poLITE تصير poLITEly. والمقاطع غير المشدَّدة تُنطق خفيفة.",
trap:"الخطأ الشائع: نقل النبر إلى آخر الكلمة («كيرفولي»). ابقَ على نبر الصفة الأصلية كما هو.",
w:[["carefully","/ˈkerfəli/"],["quickly","/ˈkwɪkli/"],["slowly","/ˈsloʊli/"],["easily","/ˈiːzəli/"],["politely","/pəˈlaɪtli/"],["clearly","/ˈklɪrli/"],["quietly","/ˈkwaɪətli/"],["correctly","/kəˈrektli/"]],
pairs:[],
say:["She speaks *clear*ly and po*lite*ly.","Please read the contract *care*fully.","He finished the report *quick*ly."]},

d24:{t:["Melody of if-sentences","نغمة الجملة الشرطية"],
how:"الجملة الشرطية مجموعتان من الكلمات. عندما تبدأ بـ if يرتفع الصوت قليلًا في آخر الجزء الأول (علامة أن الكلام لم ينتهِ)، ثم وقفة قصيرة عند الفاصلة، ثم ينخفض الصوت في آخر الجملة. وإذا جاءت if في الوسط فلا وقفة.",
trap:"الخطأ الشائع: إنزال الصوت بعد الجزء الأول فيظن السامع أنك انتهيت. ولا تنسَ ‎'ll‎ في الجزء الثاني: we'll وليس we.",
w:[["if","/ɪf/"],["rains","/reɪnz/"],["we'll","/wiːl/"],["won't","/woʊnt/"],["unless","/ənˈles/"],["umbrella","/ʌmˈbrelə/"],["weather","/ˈweðər/"],["tomorrow","/təˈmɑːroʊ/"]],
pairs:[],
say:["If it rains, we'll stay at home.","If you're late, you'll miss the bus.","I'll call you if I finish early."]},

d25:{t:["/oʊ/ and /ɑː/","الفرق بين /oʊ/ و /ɑː/"],
how:"/oʊ/ صوت مركَّب متحرك يبدأ بـ o وينتهي بضمّ الشفتين كما في go. أما حرف o القصير في النطق الأمريكي فيُنطق /ɑː/: ألف مفتوحة واسعة دون تدوير الشفتين، فكلمة hot تُسمع قريبة من «هات» و stop قريبة من «ستاب».",
trap:"الخطأ الشائع: نطق hot و not و stop بضمة كما في النطق البريطاني أو العربي، أو نطق go بصوت ثابت دون حركة الشفتين.",
w:[["go","/ɡoʊ/"],["hotel","/hoʊˈtel/"],["boat","/boʊt/"],["flown","/floʊn/"],["hot","/hɑːt/"],["stop","/stɑːp/"],["lot","/lɑːt/"],["got","/ɡɑːt/"]],
pairs:[["note","not"],["hope","hop"],["coat","cot"],["road","rod"]],
say:["Have you ever flown to Europe?","No, I've never stayed in a hotel there.","I've been on a boat, but not on the ocean."]},

d26:{t:["/dʒ/ in just, and /j/ in yet","صوت /dʒ/ في just وصوت /j/ في yet"],
how:"/dʒ/ هو الجيم المعطَّشة: يبدأ بتوقف قصير (د) ثم ينطلق، كما في just و job. أما /j/ فهو صوت الياء كما في yet و you. وصوت /ʒ/ مستمر دون توقف في أوله، كما في usually و decision.",
trap:"في القاهرة تُنطق الجيم مثل g، فتتحول just إلى «جَست» بجيم قاهرية و manager إلى «ماناجر». عطِّش الجيم دائمًا، ولا تخلط بين jet و yet.",
w:[["just","/dʒʌst/"],["job","/dʒɑːb/"],["manager","/ˈmænɪdʒər/"],["project","/ˈprɑːdʒekt/"],["change","/tʃeɪndʒ/"],["yet","/jet/"],["usually","/ˈjuːʒuəli/"],["decision","/dɪˈsɪʒn/"]],
pairs:[["jet","yet"],["cheap","jeep"],["chain","Jane"]],
say:["I've just finished the project.","The manager has already made a decision.","Have you changed your job yet?"]},

l3:{t:["The /ɜːr/ sound in work","صوت /ɜːr/ في كلمة work"],
how:"في /ɜːr/ يمتزج حرف العلة مع r في صوت واحد: اسحب لسانك إلى الخلف وثبّته، ودوّر شفتيك قليلًا. الكتابة مختلفة (er و ir و ur و or و ear) لكن الصوت واحد: work و first و learn.",
trap:"الخطأ الشائع: نطق الكلمة حسب كتابتها («وُورك»، «فِيرست»)، أو الخلط بين work و walk. في walk لا يوجد r وحرف l صامت: /wɔːk/.",
w:[["work","/wɜːrk/"],["first","/fɜːrst/"],["learn","/lɜːrn/"],["early","/ˈɜːrli/"],["person","/ˈpɜːrsn/"],["service","/ˈsɜːrvɪs/"],["world","/wɜːrld/"],["were","/wɜːr/"]],
pairs:[["walk","work"],["bed","bird"],["far","fur"],["hard","heard"]],
say:["I've worked in customer service for ten years.","I learned a lot in my first job.","I'm a person who works hard and learns fast."]},

d28:{t:["Pausing with linking words","الوقفات مع أدوات الربط"],
how:"أدوات الربط تقسّم الحكاية إلى مجموعات. بعد First و Then و Finally و Suddenly في أول الجملة: وقفة قصيرة ونغمة صاعدة قليلًا. وقبل but و so و because وقفة خفيفة. وفي وسط الجملة تُنطق because ضعيفة /bɪkəz/ و but ضعيفة /bət/.",
trap:"الخطأ الشائع: قراءة الجملة الطويلة دفعة واحدة بلا وقفات، أو تشديد but و because. الوقفة هي التي تجعل حكايتك مفهومة.",
w:[["first","/fɜːrst/"],["then","/ðen/"],["after that","/ˈæftər ðæt/"],["because","/bɪˈkɔːz/"],["so","/soʊ/"],["but","/bʌt/"],["suddenly","/ˈsʌdnli/"],["finally","/ˈfaɪnəli/"]],
pairs:[],
say:["First, I missed the bus, so I took a taxi.","I was tired, but I finished the work.","Finally, we went home, because it was late."]},

d29:{t:["Weak to after verbs","النطق الضعيف لـ to بعد الأفعال"],
how:"كلمة to قبل الفعل تُنطق ضعيفة جدًّا /tə/ وليس /tuː/، وتلتصق بالفعل الذي قبلها: want to و need to و hope to. الضغط يكون على الفعلين، و to مجرد جسر سريع بينهما.",
trap:"الخطأ الشائع: نطق to قوية وطويلة مثل الرقم two. اجعلها أقصر كلمة في الجملة.",
w:[["want to","/ˈwɑːnt tə/"],["need to","/ˈniːd tə/"],["hope to","/ˈhoʊp tə/"],["plan to","/ˈplæn tə/"],["decide to","/dɪˈsaɪd tə/"],["enjoy","/ɪnˈdʒɔɪ/"],["finish","/ˈfɪnɪʃ/"],["practice","/ˈpræktɪs/"]],
pairs:[],
say:["I *want* to im*prove* my *Eng*lish.","I *hope* to *pass* the e*xam* this *year*.","I en*joy* *learn*ing, and I *plan* to keep *go*ing."]},

d30:{t:["American rhythm: the full checklist","الإيقاع الأمريكي: مراجعة شاملة"],
how:"راجع أهم ما تعلمته في 30 يومًا: طرف اللسان بين الأسنان في th، ونَفَس الهواء مع p، وحرف R بلا طرق، وحرف T الخفيف بين حرفَي علة، والاختصارات مثل I'll، ثم الأهم: شدّد كلمات المعنى ومرّ سريعًا على الكلمات الوظيفية.",
trap:"لا تحاول إصلاح كل شيء في وقت واحد. اختر صوتًا واحدًا كل أسبوع، وسجّل صوتك بمسجّل الهاتف وقارنه بالنموذج.",
w:[["think","/θɪŋk/"],["this","/ðɪs/"],["people","/ˈpiːpəl/"],["better","/ˈbet̬ər/"],["world","/wɜːrld/"],["worked","/wɜːrkt/"],["gonna","/ˈɡʌnə/"],["I'll","/aɪl/"]],
pairs:[],
say:["I *start*ed this *jour*ney *thir*ty days a*go*.","I'm *speak*ing *bett*er than be*fore*.","I'll keep *prac*ticing *ev*ery *day*."]}
};
LESSONS.forEach(L=>{L.p=PRON[L.id]});

/* "Use It Yourself", one set per lesson.
   p    = personalise        [instruction en, instruction ar, example answer] x3
   t    = transform          [instruction en, instruction ar, source sentence, model answer] x3
   q    = real-life response [question, question ar, model answer, useful words] x3
   rp   = role-play          [situation en, situation ar, [A, B, A, B ...]]  (the learner speaks the B lines)
   talk = 30-60 second task  [task en, task ar, useful words, model answer] */
const USE={
l1:{p:[
["Say what time you really wake up on workdays.","قل متى تستيقظ فعلًا في أيام العمل.","I wake up at five thirty on workdays."],
["Say what you usually have for breakfast.","قل ماذا تتناول عادةً على الإفطار.","I usually have cheese, bread, and a cup of coffee."],
["Say how you go to work.","قل كيف تذهب إلى العمل.","I go to work by car, and it takes about forty minutes."]],
t:[
["Change the sentence to talk about your manager (he or she).","غيّر الجملة لتتحدث عن مديرك (he أو she).","I arrive at the office at half past eight.","She arrives at the office at half past eight."],
["Make it negative.","حوّلها إلى النفي.","I check my phone for new messages.","I don't check my phone for new messages."],
["Make a question with \"you\".","كوّن سؤالًا باستخدام you.","I drive my kids to school first.","Do you drive your kids to school first?"]],
q:[
["What do you do before you go to work?","ماذا تفعل قبل الذهاب إلى العمل؟","I take a shower, get dressed, and have a quick breakfast.","take a shower · get dressed · have breakfast"],
["How long does it take you to get to work?","كم يستغرق وصولك إلى العمل؟","It usually takes about forty minutes, but the traffic is often heavy.","it takes · about · traffic"],
["What time do you start work, and what do you do first?","متى تبدأ العمل، وما أول شيء تفعله؟","I start at half past eight. First, I check my email.","start at · first · check"]],
rp:["A new colleague asks about your morning. Answer each question.","زميل جديد يسألك عن صباحك. أجب عن كل سؤال.",
["Good morning! You're early. What time do you get up?","I get up at six. I like a quiet start to the day.","Do you have breakfast at home or at work?","At home. I usually have breakfast with my family."]],
talk:["Describe your morning from the moment you wake up until you arrive at work. Do not read.","صِف صباحك من لحظة استيقاظك حتى وصولك إلى العمل. دون قراءة.","wake up · then · usually · leave · arrive",
"I wake up at six every day. First, I take a shower and get dressed. Then I have breakfast with my family. I usually have eggs and tea. We leave the house at seven thirty. I drive my children to school, and then I go to work. The traffic is often heavy, so I listen to English in the car. I arrive at the office at half past eight."]},

d02:{p:[
["Say your name and where you are from.","قل اسمك ومن أين أنت.","My name is Mahmoud, and I'm from Giza, in Egypt."],
["Say your job and where you work.","قل وظيفتك ومكان عملك.","I'm a product manager at a bank."],
["Say if your office is near your home or far from it.","قل هل مكتبك قريب من بيتك أم بعيد عنه.","My office isn't near my home. It's about forty minutes away."]],
t:[
["Make it negative.","حوّلها إلى النفي.","She's an accountant.","She isn't an accountant."],
["Make a question.","كوّن سؤالًا.","They're in the same department.","Are they in the same department?"],
["Change \"I\" to \"we\".","غيّر I إلى we.","I'm new here.","We're new here."]],
q:[
["Where are you from, and what's your job?","من أين أنت، وما وظيفتك؟","I'm from Egypt, and I'm a manager at a bank.","I'm from · I'm a"],
["Are you new in this team?","هل أنت جديد في هذا الفريق؟","No, I'm not. I've been here for a few years.","Yes, I am · No, I'm not"],
["Who is the person next to you?","من الشخص الذي بجوارك؟","This is my colleague, Mona. She's an accountant.","This is · He's · She's"]],
rp:["You meet a visitor at a meeting. Introduce yourself and answer.","تقابل زائرًا في اجتماع. عرّف بنفسك وأجب.",
["Hello, I'm Anna from the Milan office. Nice to meet you.","Nice to meet you, Anna. I'm Mahmoud. I'm a product manager here.","Are you from Cairo?","I'm from Giza. It's very near Cairo."]],
talk:["Introduce yourself and one colleague to a new team.","عرّف بنفسك وبأحد زملائك لفريق جديد.","my name is · I'm from · I'm a · this is · he's / she's",
"Hello, everyone. My name is Mahmoud, and I'm from Egypt. I'm a product manager at a bank. I'm in the retail department. This is my colleague, Mona. She's an accountant, and she's very friendly. We're in the same building, but we aren't in the same team. It's a pleasure to meet you all."]},

d03:{p:[
["Say how many brothers and sisters you have.","قل كم أخًا وأختًا لك.","I have one brother and two sisters."],
["Say one thing about a family member, using his or her.","قل شيئًا عن أحد أفراد أسرتك مستخدمًا his أو her.","My daughter is ten, and her favorite subject is science."],
["Say where your parents live.","قل أين يعيش والداك.","My parents live in a small town near Tanta."]],
t:[
["Use 's instead of \"of\".","استخدم ‎'s‎ بدلًا من of.","the car of my brother","my brother's car"],
["Change \"my son\" to \"my daughter\".","غيّر my son إلى my daughter.","My son loves his school.","My daughter loves her school."],
["Change \"I\" to \"we\".","غيّر I إلى we.","I visit my parents every Friday.","We visit our parents every Friday."]],
q:[
["Do you have a big family?","هل أسرتك كبيرة؟","Yes, I do. I have three children and a lot of cousins.","I have · children · cousins"],
["Who is the oldest person in your family?","من أكبر شخص في أسرتك؟","My grandmother is the oldest. She's eighty-five.","my grandmother · my father · the oldest"],
["Whose phone is this?","هاتف من هذا؟","It's my wife's phone.","It's my … 's"]],
rp:["A colleague sees a family photo on your desk.","زميل يرى صورة أسرتك على مكتبك.",
["Is this your family? What a lovely photo!","Thank you. Yes, this is my wife, and these are our children.","How old is your son?","He's twelve, and his sister is nine."]],
talk:["Describe your family: who they are, their ages or jobs, and where they live.","صِف أسرتك: من هم، وأعمارهم أو وظائفهم، وأين يعيشون.","my · his · her · their · 's",
"I have a big family. My wife's name is Dina, and she's a teacher. We have two sons and a daughter. Our older son is in high school, and his favorite subject is math. Our daughter is the youngest. My parents live in a small village, and their house has a big garden. We visit them every month. My family is very important to me."]},

d04:{p:[
["Say what kind of home you live in and on which floor.","قل ما نوع مسكنك وفي أي طابق.","I live in an apartment on the fifth floor."],
["Say how many rooms there are.","قل كم غرفة فيه.","There are three bedrooms and a big living room."],
["Say one thing there isn't in your home.","قل شيئًا غير موجود في بيتك.","There isn't a balcony, but there's a lot of light."]],
t:[
["Make it negative.","حوّلها إلى النفي.","There's a garden.","There isn't a garden."],
["Make it plural with \"two\".","حوّلها إلى الجمع مع two.","There's a bathroom.","There are two bathrooms."],
["Make a question.","كوّن سؤالًا.","There's an elevator in the building.","Is there an elevator in the building?"]],
q:[
["Is there a supermarket near your home?","هل يوجد سوبر ماركت قرب بيتك؟","Yes, there is. There's one across the street.","Yes, there is · No, there isn't"],
["What is there in your living room?","ماذا يوجد في غرفة المعيشة عندك؟","There's a sofa, a table, and a big TV.","there's · there are"],
["Are there any parks in your area?","هل توجد حدائق في منطقتك؟","There aren't any big parks, but there's a small one nearby.","there are · there aren't any"]],
rp:["You call an agent about an apartment. Ask and react.","تتصل بوسيط عقاري بخصوص شقة. اسأل وتفاعل.",
["Hello, the apartment is still available. It's on the second floor.","Great. How many bedrooms are there?","There are two bedrooms and one bathroom.","Is there a parking space?"]],
talk:["Describe your home room by room, and say what there is near it.","صِف بيتك غرفةً غرفة، واذكر ما يوجد بالقرب منه.","there's · there are · next to · near · but",
"I live in an apartment on the third floor. There are three bedrooms and two bathrooms. There's a big living room with a balcony. The kitchen is small, but it's modern. There isn't a garden, but there's a park nearby. There are also some shops across the street. It's not a big home, but it's comfortable, and I like it."]},

d05:{p:[
["Say three things you need from the supermarket this week.","اذكر ثلاثة أشياء تحتاجها من السوبر ماركت هذا الأسبوع.","I need some rice, some chicken, and a bottle of oil."],
["Say one thing you don't have at home right now.","اذكر شيئًا ليس عندك في البيت الآن.","We don't have any bread at home."],
["Say how much water you drink a day.","قل كم تشرب من الماء يوميًّا.","I drink about two liters of water a day."]],
t:[
["Make it negative with \"any\".","حوّلها إلى النفي باستخدام any.","We have some milk.","We don't have any milk."],
["Ask about the quantity.","اسأل عن الكمية.","We need rice.","How much rice do we need?"],
["Ask about the number.","اسأل عن العدد.","There are eggs in the box.","How many eggs are there in the box?"]],
q:[
["How much sugar do you take in your tea?","كم تضع من السكر في الشاي؟","Not much. Just one spoon.","not much · a lot · one spoon"],
["How many people do you cook for?","لكم شخص تطبخ؟","I cook for five people.","how many · I cook for"],
["Can I help you find something?","هل أساعدك في العثور على شيء؟","Yes, please. Where can I find the olive oil?","Where can I find · Do you have any"]],
rp:["You are at the cheese counter. Ask for what you want.","أنت عند قسم الأجبان. اطلب ما تريد.",
["Good evening. What can I get you?","Can I have some white cheese, please?","Sure. How much would you like?","Half a kilo, please. And how much is it?"]],
talk:["You are planning dinner for guests. Say what you have, what you don't have, and what you need to buy.","تخطط لعشاء ضيوف. قل ما عندك وما ليس عندك وما تحتاج إلى شرائه.","some · any · much · many · a kilo of · a bottle of",
"I'm cooking dinner for six people on Friday. I have some rice and some vegetables at home, but I don't have any chicken. I also need a bottle of oil and some bread. There isn't much sugar left, so I'll buy a kilo. I don't need many sweets, just a small cake. I'm going to the supermarket this evening."]},

d06:{p:[
["Say what you are doing right now.","قل ماذا تفعل الآن.","I'm practicing my English right now."],
["Say what you are working on this week.","قل على ماذا تعمل هذا الأسبوع.","I'm working on a new product this week."],
["Say what someone near you is doing.","قل ماذا يفعل شخص قريب منك الآن.","My colleague is talking on the phone."]],
t:[
["Make it negative.","حوّلها إلى النفي.","The printer is working.","The printer isn't working."],
["Make a question with \"what\".","كوّن سؤالًا باستخدام what.","She's writing an email.","What is she writing?"],
["Change \"I\" to \"they\".","غيّر I إلى they.","I'm having lunch.","They're having lunch."]],
q:[
["Are you busy at the moment?","هل أنت مشغول الآن؟","Yes, I am. I'm finishing a report.","Yes, I am · I'm …ing"],
["What is your team working on this month?","على ماذا يعمل فريقك هذا الشهر؟","We're preparing a new offer for customers.","we're …ing"],
["Why isn't he answering his phone?","لماذا لا يرد على هاتفه؟","He's in a meeting right now.","he's …ing · right now"]],
rp:["Your manager calls while you are busy.","مديرك يتصل بك وأنت مشغول.",
["Hi, are you free? I need the sales numbers.","I'm working on them right now.","Good. When can you send them?","I'm checking the last page. I'll send them in ten minutes."]],
talk:["Describe what is happening in your office (or home) right now. Mention at least four people or things.","صِف ما يحدث في مكتبك (أو بيتك) الآن. اذكر أربعة أشخاص أو أشياء على الأقل.","is …ing · are …ing · right now · at the moment",
"It's a busy day at the office. I'm working on a report right now. My manager is talking to a client in the meeting room. Two colleagues are preparing slides for tomorrow. The printer isn't working, so someone is calling the IT department. Everyone is working hard because we're launching a new product this month."]},

d07:{p:[
["Say what you usually do on Fridays.","قل ماذا تفعل عادةً يوم الجمعة.","I usually visit my parents on Fridays."],
["Say what is different this week.","قل ما المختلف هذا الأسبوع.","This Friday I'm staying at home because I'm tired."],
["Say a hobby you enjoy.","اذكر هواية تستمتع بها.","I enjoy walking and listening to podcasts."]],
t:[
["Change it to \"right now\".","غيّرها لتدل على الآن.","She reads novels.","She's reading a novel right now."],
["Change it to \"every day\".","غيّرها لتدل على العادة اليومية.","I'm practicing English now.","I practice English every day."],
["Make it negative.","حوّلها إلى النفي.","My brother likes swimming.","My brother doesn't like swimming."]],
q:[
["What do you do in your free time?","ماذا تفعل في وقت فراغك؟","I watch football and spend time with my family.","I play · I watch · I enjoy …ing"],
["What are you doing this weekend?","ماذا ستفعل في عطلة هذا الأسبوع؟","I'm taking my children to the club.","I'm …ing this weekend"],
["Do you prefer staying at home or going out?","هل تفضّل البقاء في البيت أم الخروج؟","I prefer going out, but this week I'm resting.","I prefer …ing"]],
rp:["A colleague invites you to play football.","زميل يدعوك للعب كرة القدم.",
["We play football every Thursday. Do you play?","Yes, I do. I usually play on Fridays.","Great. Are you coming this Thursday?","I'm sorry, I can't. I'm working late this week."]],
talk:["Talk about your free time: what you usually do, and what you are doing differently this week.","تحدّث عن وقت فراغك: ما تفعله عادةً، وما تفعله بشكل مختلف هذا الأسبوع.","usually · every · but this week · right now · I enjoy",
"In my free time, I usually play football with my friends on Fridays. I also enjoy reading and listening to podcasts. My wife loves cooking, and our children watch cartoons in the evening. But this week is different. I'm not playing football because I'm tired. I'm staying at home, and I'm learning English every day."]},

d08:{p:[
["Order your favorite drink politely.","اطلب مشروبك المفضل بأدب.","I'd like a mint tea, please."],
["Say what you would like for lunch today.","قل ماذا تودّ أن تتناول على الغداء اليوم.","I'd like grilled chicken with rice."],
["Offer a guest something to drink.","اعرض على ضيف شيئًا يشربه.","Would you like some coffee or tea?"]],
t:[
["Make it more polite with \"would like\".","اجعلها أكثر تهذيبًا باستخدام would like.","I want the menu.","I'd like the menu, please."],
["Change it into an offer.","حوّلها إلى عرض.","Do you want some dessert?","Would you like some dessert?"],
["Change \"I\" to \"we\".","غيّر I إلى we.","I'd like a table by the window.","We'd like a table by the window."]],
q:[
["Would you like anything to drink?","هل تودّ أن تشرب شيئًا؟","Yes, please. I'd like a bottle of water.","Yes, please · I'd like · No, thank you"],
["How would you like your coffee?","كيف تحب قهوتك؟","With a little sugar and no milk, please.","with · without · a little"],
["Would you like to pay by cash or card?","هل تودّ الدفع نقدًا أم بالبطاقة؟","By card, please.","by card · in cash"]],
rp:["You are at a restaurant with a client. Order for both of you.","أنت في مطعم مع عميل. اطلب لكما.",
["Good evening. Are you ready to order?","Yes. I'd like the grilled fish, and my guest would like the chicken.","Certainly. And to drink?","We'd like two orange juices, please."]],
talk:["You are in a restaurant. Ask for a table, order a starter, a main course and a drink, then ask for the check.","أنت في مطعم. اطلب طاولة، ثم مقبّلات وطبقًا رئيسيًّا ومشروبًا، ثم اطلب الحساب.","a table for · I'd like · could we have · the check",
"Good evening. A table for two, please. We'd like to see the menu. To start, I'd like the lentil soup. For the main course, I'd like the grilled chicken with rice and salad. And I'd like a fresh orange juice, please. Could we have some more bread? Everything is delicious. Could we have the check, please? Thank you very much."]},

d09:{p:[
["Compare two shops you know.","قارن بين متجرين تعرفهما.","The mall is bigger than the shop near my home, but it's more expensive."],
["Compare your phone with your old one.","قارن هاتفك بهاتفك القديم.","My new phone is faster than my old one."],
["Say which is easier for you: shopping online or in stores.","قل أيهما أسهل لك: التسوق عبر الإنترنت أم في المتاجر.","Shopping online is easier, but stores are better for clothes."]],
t:[
["Use the comparative.","استخدم صيغة المقارنة.","This jacket is cheap. (than that one)","This jacket is cheaper than that one."],
["Use the comparative.","استخدم صيغة المقارنة.","Cotton is comfortable. (than wool)","Cotton is more comfortable than wool."],
["Say the opposite.","قل العكس.","The blue shirt is bigger than the white one.","The white shirt is smaller than the blue one."]],
q:[
["Which is better for work, a jacket or a sweater?","أيهما أفضل للعمل: الجاكيت أم السترة الصوفية؟","A jacket is better. It looks more professional.","better · more professional"],
["Is this size OK for you?","هل هذا المقاس مناسب لك؟","It's a bit tight. Do you have a larger size?","a bit tight · a larger size"],
["Why do you prefer this brand?","لماذا تفضّل هذه العلامة؟","The quality is better, and it lasts longer.","better · longer · cheaper"]],
rp:["You are buying shoes. Ask for what you need.","أنت تشتري حذاءً. اطلب ما تحتاجه.",
["These are our most popular shoes. How do they feel?","They're a bit tight. Do you have a bigger size?","Yes, here you are. These are a size larger.","These are more comfortable. Are they more expensive?"]],
talk:["Compare two products you could buy (two phones, two cars or two jackets) and say which one you will choose.","قارن بين منتجين يمكنك شراؤهما (هاتفان أو سيارتان أو جاكيتان) وقل أيهما ستختار.","cheaper · more expensive · better · bigger · than",
"I'm looking for a new phone. The first one is cheaper, and it's lighter than the second one. The second phone is more expensive, but its camera is better, and the screen is bigger. The battery also lasts longer. Quality is more important than price for me, so I'll take the second one."]},

d10:{p:[
["Say which is the best restaurant you know.","قل ما أفضل مطعم تعرفه.","The best restaurant I know is a small fish place in Alexandria."],
["Say which is the busiest day of your week.","قل ما أكثر أيام أسبوعك ازدحامًا.","Sunday is the busiest day of my week."],
["Say which is the most beautiful place in your country.","قل ما أجمل مكان في بلدك.","I think the most beautiful place in Egypt is Aswan."]],
t:[
["Use the superlative.","استخدم صيغة التفضيل.","This street is famous. (in the area)","This is the most famous street in the area."],
["Use the superlative.","استخدم صيغة التفضيل.","The metro is a cheap way to travel.","The metro is the cheapest way to travel."],
["Make a question with \"which\".","كوّن سؤالًا باستخدام which.","This is the tallest building in town.","Which is the tallest building in town?"]],
q:[
["What's the best way to get around your city?","ما أفضل وسيلة للتنقل في مدينتك؟","The fastest way is by metro, and it's also the cheapest.","the fastest · the cheapest · by metro"],
["What's the worst time to drive?","ما أسوأ وقت للقيادة؟","The worst time is between four and six in the afternoon.","the worst time · rush hour"],
["Where should a visitor go first?","إلى أين يذهب الزائر أولًا؟","The museum is the most interesting place for visitors.","the most interesting · the oldest"]],
rp:["A visitor from another office asks you for advice.","زائر من مكتب آخر يطلب نصيحتك.",
["It's my first time in Cairo. What should I see?","The pyramids are the most famous place, of course.","And where can I eat good local food?","The best restaurant near here is two streets away."]],
talk:["Recommend your city to a visitor: the best places, the best time to visit, and the best way to travel.","رشّح مدينتك لزائر: أفضل الأماكن، وأفضل وقت للزيارة، وأفضل وسيلة للتنقل.","the best · the most · the cheapest · the oldest · in the city",
"Cairo is the biggest city in Egypt, and it's also the busiest. The most famous place is the pyramids, and the best view of the Nile is from the bridges at night. The cheapest way to travel is by metro. Winter is the best time to visit because summer is the hottest season. Friday morning is the quietest time in the city."]},

d11:{p:[
["Say how to get from your home to the nearest shop.","قل كيف تصل من بيتك إلى أقرب متجر.","Go out of the building, turn right, and it's on the corner."],
["Say where your office is.","قل أين يقع مكتبك.","My office is opposite a big bank, next to a pharmacy."],
["Tell a driver where to stop.","قل للسائق أين يتوقف.","Please stop here, just before the traffic lights."]],
t:[
["Make it negative.","حوّلها إلى النفي.","Turn right at the square.","Don't turn right at the square."],
["Make it more polite with \"please\".","اجعلها أكثر تهذيبًا باستخدام please.","Slow down.","Please slow down."],
["Change \"left\" to \"right\" and \"second\" to \"first\".","غيّر left إلى right و second إلى first.","Take the second street on the left.","Take the first street on the right."]],
q:[
["Excuse me, is there a bank near here?","من فضلك، هل يوجد بنك قريب من هنا؟","Yes, there is. Go straight ahead, and it's on the left.","go straight · on the left · on the right"],
["How far is the station?","كم تبعد المحطة؟","It's about ten minutes on foot.","about · on foot · by car"],
["Which floor is your office on?","في أي طابق مكتبك؟","It's on the fourth floor. Take the elevator and turn left.","on the … floor · take the elevator"]],
rp:["A visitor calls you from the street. Guide him to your office.","زائر يتصل بك من الشارع. أرشده إلى مكتبك.",
["Hi, I'm at the metro station. How do I get to your office?","Go out of the station and turn left.","OK. And then?","Walk past the bank. Our building is opposite the mosque."]],
talk:["Give clear directions from a place everyone knows to your office or home. Use at least five steps.","أعطِ اتجاهات واضحة من مكان معروف إلى مكتبك أو بيتك. استخدم خمس خطوات على الأقل.","go straight · turn · take · walk past · it's opposite / next to",
"From the metro station, go straight ahead for two blocks. Turn left at the traffic lights. Then take the second street on the right. Walk past the bank and the bakery. Cross the road at the crosswalk. My office is opposite the big mosque, next to a gas station. Don't go into the first building. The entrance is behind it. It's about ten minutes on foot."]},

d12:{p:[
["Say how you feel today.","قل كيف تشعر اليوم.","I feel fine today, but I'm a little tired."],
["Give yourself one piece of health advice.","قدّم لنفسك نصيحة صحية واحدة.","I should sleep earlier and drink more water."],
["Say one thing you shouldn't do before bed.","اذكر شيئًا لا ينبغي أن تفعله قبل النوم.","I shouldn't use my phone before bed."]],
t:[
["Make it negative.","حوّلها إلى النفي.","You should go to work tomorrow.","You shouldn't go to work tomorrow."],
["Make a question.","كوّن سؤالًا.","I should stay in bed.","Should I stay in bed?"],
["Give the advice with \"should\".","قدّم النصيحة باستخدام should.","Drink plenty of water.","You should drink plenty of water."]],
q:[
["What seems to be the problem?","ما المشكلة التي تشكو منها؟","I have a bad headache, and I can't sleep.","I have a · I can't"],
["My friend has a cold. What should he do?","صديقي مصاب بنزلة برد. ماذا ينبغي أن يفعل؟","He should rest and drink hot drinks. He shouldn't go out.","he should · he shouldn't"],
["How often should I take this medicine?","كم مرة ينبغي أن أتناول هذا الدواء؟","You should take it twice a day, after meals.","twice a day · after meals"]],
rp:["You call your manager because you are sick.","تتصل بمديرك لأنك مريض.",
["Good morning. You don't sound well.","I'm sorry, I have a fever. I don't think I should come in today.","Of course. You should rest. Do you need anything?","No, thank you. I should feel better in two days."]],
talk:["A colleague is very tired and stressed. Give him or her five pieces of advice.","زميل متعب ومضغوط جدًّا. قدّم له خمس نصائح.","you should · you shouldn't · I think",
"You look very tired. I think you should take a few days off. You should sleep at least seven hours a night, and you shouldn't work late every day. You should drink plenty of water and eat healthy food. You shouldn't drink too much coffee. And you should see a doctor if you don't feel better next week."]},

d13:{p:[
["Say where you were yesterday evening.","قل أين كنت مساء أمس.","I was at home with my family yesterday evening."],
["Say how your last weekend was.","قل كيف كانت عطلتك الماضية.","It was quiet and relaxing."],
["Say something about your first job.","قل شيئًا عن أول وظيفة لك.","My first job was in sales, and I was twenty-two."]],
t:[
["Change it to the past.","حوّلها إلى الماضي.","The weather is cold and windy.","The weather was cold and windy."],
["Make it negative.","حوّلها إلى النفي.","They were at the branch.","They weren't at the branch."],
["Make a question.","كوّن سؤالًا.","The meeting was useful.","Was the meeting useful?"]],
q:[
["Where were you at eight o'clock this morning?","أين كنت في الثامنة صباح اليوم؟","I was in my car, on the way to work.","I was in / at / on"],
["How was the traffic today?","كيف كان الزحام اليوم؟","It was terrible. I was twenty minutes late.","it was · I was late"],
["Were you at the meeting yesterday?","هل كنت في اجتماع أمس؟","No, I wasn't. I was with a customer.","Yes, I was · No, I wasn't"]],
rp:["A colleague asks why you were not at the office yesterday.","زميل يسألك لماذا لم تكن في المكتب أمس.",
["We missed you yesterday. Where were you?","I was at the head office all day.","Oh, was it a training day?","Yes, it was. It was long, but it was useful."]],
talk:["Describe yesterday: where you were in the morning, afternoon and evening, who you were with, and how it was.","صِف يوم أمس: أين كنت صباحًا وظهرًا ومساءً، ومع من كنت، وكيف كان اليوم.","I was · we were · it was · there was · there were",
"Yesterday was a long day. In the morning, I was at the office, and there were a lot of customers. My colleagues were very busy too. In the afternoon, I was in a meeting for two hours. It was useful, but I was tired. In the evening, I was at home with my family. The children were happy, and it was a wonderful evening in the end."]},

d14:{p:[
["Say one thing you watched last week.","اذكر شيئًا شاهدته الأسبوع الماضي.","I watched a football match last Friday."],
["Say who you visited or called last weekend.","قل من زرت أو كلّمت في العطلة الماضية.","I visited my parents and called my brother."],
["Say what time you finished work yesterday.","قل متى أنهيت عملك أمس.","I finished work at six yesterday."]],
t:[
["Change it to the past.","حوّلها إلى الماضي.","I clean the car on Fridays.","I cleaned the car last Friday."],
["Change it to the past.","حوّلها إلى الماضي.","We talk for two hours.","We talked for two hours."],
["Change \"I\" to \"she\".","غيّر I إلى she.","I decided to sleep early.","She decided to sleep early."]],
q:[
["What did you do last weekend?","ماذا فعلت في العطلة الماضية؟","I stayed at home and watched a movie with my family.","I stayed · I watched · I visited"],
["Who cooked dinner yesterday?","من أعدّ العشاء أمس؟","My wife cooked, and I helped her.","cooked · helped"],
["When did you start your current job?","متى بدأت وظيفتك الحالية؟","I started in June.","I started in"]],
rp:["Monday morning. A colleague asks about your weekend.","صباح أول يوم عمل. زميل يسألك عن عطلتك.",
["Good morning! How was your weekend?","It was great. We invited my parents for lunch.","That sounds nice. Did you cook?","No, my wife cooked. I washed the dishes!"]],
talk:["Describe your last weekend from Friday morning to Saturday night. Use at least six past verbs.","صِف عطلتك الماضية من صباح الجمعة إلى ليل السبت. استخدم ستة أفعال ماضية على الأقل.","stayed · visited · watched · cooked · talked · finished",
"Last weekend I stayed at home. On Friday morning, I washed the car and cleaned the garage. We invited my parents for lunch, and my wife cooked a big meal. After lunch, we talked for two hours. In the evening, we watched an old movie. On Saturday, I visited a friend, and then I helped my daughter with her homework. I enjoyed a quiet weekend."]},

d15:{p:[
["Say where you went on your last trip.","قل إلى أين ذهبت في آخر رحلة لك.","I went to the North Coast last summer."],
["Say what you ate yesterday.","قل ماذا أكلت أمس.","I had fish and rice for lunch yesterday."],
["Say something you bought last month.","اذكر شيئًا اشتريته الشهر الماضي.","I bought a new pair of shoes last month."]],
t:[
["Change it to the past.","حوّلها إلى الماضي.","We go to Alexandria by train.","We went to Alexandria by train."],
["Change it to the past.","حوّلها إلى الماضي.","I meet my friends and we have lunch.","I met my friends and we had lunch."],
["Change it to the past.","حوّلها إلى الماضي.","She takes a lot of photos.","She took a lot of photos."]],
q:[
["How did you get there?","كيف وصلت إلى هناك؟","We went by car. It took about three hours.","went by · it took"],
["What did you see on your trip?","ماذا رأيت في رحلتك؟","We saw the old city and the sea.","we saw · we went to"],
["Did you buy anything?","هل اشتريت شيئًا؟","Yes, I bought some gifts for my family.","I bought · I didn't buy"]],
rp:["A colleague asks about your holiday.","زميل يسألك عن إجازتك.",
["Welcome back! Where did you go?","We went to Alexandria for three days.","Lovely. What did you do there?","We swam in the sea and ate a lot of fresh fish."]],
talk:["Tell the story of a trip you took: where you went, how you got there, what you saw, ate and bought, and when you came back.","احكِ عن رحلة قمت بها: إلى أين ذهبت، وكيف وصلت، وماذا رأيت وأكلت واشتريت، ومتى عدت.","went · left · took · saw · ate · bought · came back",
"Last month we went to Alexandria by train. We left Cairo at seven in the morning, and the trip took about three hours. We got to the hotel at noon. We had fresh fish for lunch by the sea. In the afternoon, we saw the famous library, and I bought some gifts for my parents. We spent two nights there and came back on Sunday. It was the best trip of the year."]},

d16:{p:[
["Say one thing you didn't do yesterday.","اذكر شيئًا لم تفعله أمس.","I didn't go to the gym yesterday."],
["Say something that went wrong last week.","اذكر شيئًا سار على غير ما يرام الأسبوع الماضي.","My laptop crashed, and I lost an hour of work."],
["Say what time you got home last night.","قل متى وصلت إلى البيت ليلة أمس.","I got home at eight last night."]],
t:[
["Make it negative.","حوّلها إلى النفي.","I heard my alarm.","I didn't hear my alarm."],
["Make a question.","كوّن سؤالًا.","You saved a copy.","Did you save a copy?"],
["Make a question with \"what\".","كوّن سؤالًا باستخدام what.","The manager said something.","What did the manager say?"]],
q:[
["Did you get to work on time today?","هل وصلت إلى العمل في موعدك اليوم؟","No, I didn't. I arrived ten minutes late.","Yes, I did · No, I didn't"],
["Why didn't you call me?","لماذا لم تتصل بي؟","I'm sorry. I didn't have your number.","I didn't have · I couldn't"],
["How did you fix the problem?","كيف حللت المشكلة؟","I called the IT department, and they fixed it.","I called · they fixed"]],
rp:["Your manager asks why a report is late.","مديرك يسألك لماذا تأخر تقرير.",
["I didn't get the report yesterday. What happened?","I'm sorry. My computer crashed, and I lost the file.","Did you save a copy?","Unfortunately, I didn't. But I wrote it again, and it's ready now."]],
talk:["Describe a day when everything went wrong. Include at least three things you didn't do and one question someone asked you.","صِف يومًا سار فيه كل شيء على غير ما يرام. اذكر ثلاثة أشياء على الأقل لم تفعلها وسؤالًا وجّهه إليك أحدهم.","I didn't · I couldn't · Did you…? · unfortunately · luckily",
"Yesterday was a terrible day. I didn't hear my alarm, so I woke up late. I didn't have time for breakfast, and I missed the bus. I arrived forty minutes late. My manager asked, \"Did you call the client?\" Unfortunately, I didn't. Then my computer crashed. Luckily, a colleague helped me. I didn't leave the office until eight."]},

d17:{p:[
["Say what you were doing at nine o'clock last night.","قل ماذا كنت تفعل في التاسعة ليلة أمس.","I was watching the news at nine last night."],
["Say what your family was doing when you got home yesterday.","قل ماذا كانت أسرتك تفعل عندما وصلت إلى البيت أمس.","When I got home, the kids were doing their homework."],
["Say what you were doing when your phone last rang.","قل ماذا كنت تفعل عندما رنّ هاتفك آخر مرة.","I was driving when my phone rang."]],
t:[
["Change it to the past continuous.","حوّلها إلى الماضي المستمر.","My wife cooks dinner.","My wife was cooking dinner."],
["Make it negative.","حوّلها إلى النفي.","I was driving fast.","I wasn't driving fast."],
["Join the two with \"when\".","اربط الجملتين باستخدام when.","I was reading. The lights went out.","I was reading when the lights went out."]],
q:[
["What were you doing at this time yesterday?","ماذا كنت تفعل في مثل هذا الوقت أمس؟","I was sitting in a meeting.","I was …ing"],
["Were you sleeping when I called?","هل كنت نائمًا عندما اتصلت؟","No, I wasn't. I was having dinner.","No, I wasn't · I was …ing"],
["What was happening when you arrived?","ماذا كان يحدث عندما وصلت؟","People were waiting outside, and it was raining.","were …ing · was …ing"]],
rp:["A colleague asks why you didn't answer the phone last night.","زميل يسألك لماذا لم ترد على الهاتف ليلة أمس.",
["I called you at eight last night, but you didn't answer.","I'm sorry. I was driving home.","In that rain? Was the road OK?","It was wet, so I wasn't driving fast."]],
talk:["Tell a short story about something that happened suddenly. Say what everyone was doing when it happened.","احكِ قصة قصيرة عن شيء حدث فجأة. قل ماذا كان الجميع يفعلون عندما حدث.","was …ing · were …ing · when · while · suddenly",
"Last night I was watching a match when the lights went out. My wife was cooking dinner, and the kids were doing their homework. It was raining heavily outside. While I was looking for a candle, my phone rang. It was my brother. He was driving home, and the road was dark. The power came back while we were eating dinner."]},

d18:{p:[
["Say what you are going to do this evening.","قل ماذا ستفعل هذا المساء.","I'm going to study English for an hour this evening."],
["Say where you are going to spend your next holiday.","قل أين ستقضي إجازتك القادمة.","We're going to spend a week by the sea."],
["Say one thing you are not going to do this weekend.","اذكر شيئًا لن تفعله في عطلة هذا الأسبوع.","I'm not going to check my work email."]],
t:[
["Make it negative.","حوّلها إلى النفي.","I'm going to rent a car.","I'm not going to rent a car."],
["Make a question.","كوّن سؤالًا.","They're going to fly.","Are they going to fly?"],
["Change \"I\" to \"my wife\".","غيّر I إلى my wife.","I'm going to choose the hotel.","My wife is going to choose the hotel."]],
q:[
["What are you going to do after work?","ماذا ستفعل بعد العمل؟","I'm going to pick up my kids and go home.","I'm going to"],
["Are you going to take any time off this summer?","هل ستأخذ إجازة هذا الصيف؟","Yes, I am. I'm going to take a week off in August.","Yes, I am · No, I'm not"],
["Who is going to do your work while you are away?","من سيقوم بعملك أثناء غيابك؟","My colleague is going to cover for me.","is going to"]],
rp:["A colleague asks about your summer plans.","زميل يسألك عن خطط الصيف.",
["Do you have any plans for the summer?","Yes. We're going to travel to Sharm El-Sheikh in August.","Nice! Are you going to drive?","No, we're going to fly. It's faster."]],
talk:["Describe your plans for your next holiday or your next free weekend: where, when, who with, and what you are going to do.","صِف خططك لإجازتك القادمة أو عطلتك القادمة: أين، ومتى، ومع من، وماذا ستفعل.","I'm going to · we're going to · I'm not going to",
"We're going to take a week off in August. We're going to fly to Sharm El-Sheikh, and I'm going to book the tickets tonight. My wife is going to choose the hotel. The kids are going to learn to dive, and I'm going to relax on the beach. I'm not going to check my email. It's going to be very hot, so we're going to pack light clothes."]},

d19:{p:[
["Make a promise about your English.","قدّم وعدًا يخص لغتك الإنجليزية.","I'll practice for thirty minutes every day."],
["Say what you think will happen at work next month.","قل ما تتوقع حدوثه في العمل الشهر القادم.","I think we'll launch the new product next month."],
["Say something you won't do tomorrow.","اذكر شيئًا لن تفعله غدًا.","I won't stay late at the office tomorrow."]],
t:[
["Make it negative.","حوّلها إلى النفي.","I'll forget.","I won't forget."],
["Make a question.","كوّن سؤالًا.","The manager will approve the budget.","Will the manager approve the budget?"],
["Offer to help.","اعرض المساعدة.","Those boxes look heavy.","I'll help you with those boxes."]],
q:[
["Can you send me the file today?","هل يمكنك أن ترسل لي الملف اليوم؟","Sure. I'll send it before noon.","I'll · before · by"],
["Will you be at the meeting tomorrow?","هل ستحضر اجتماع الغد؟","Yes, I will. I'll be there at nine.","Yes, I will · No, I won't"],
["The phone is ringing, and I'm busy.","الهاتف يرن وأنا مشغول.","Don't worry. I'll get it.","I'll get it · I'll answer"]],
rp:["A customer is waiting for an answer about a request.","عميل ينتظر ردًّا على طلب قدّمه.",
["I sent my request last week, and nobody has called me.","I'm very sorry. I'll check it right now.","Thank you. When will I get an answer?","I'll call you back before the end of the day. I promise."]],
talk:["You are starting a new task for your manager. Say what you will do, when you will finish, and what you won't do.","أنت تبدأ مهمة جديدة لمديرك. قل ماذا ستفعل، ومتى ستنتهي، وما الذي لن تفعله.","I'll · I won't · I think · I promise · by",
"Thank you for giving me this project. I'll start today. First, I'll call the client and confirm the meeting. Then I'll prepare the slides, and I'll send them to you by Wednesday. I think the project will finish on time, and we won't need extra staff. I'll let you know as soon as I hear from the client. I promise I won't be late."]},

l2:{p:[
["Ask politely for information you need at a bank.","اطلب بأدب معلومة تحتاجها في بنك.","Could you tell me the opening hours, please?"],
["Say one thing you have to do at work every day.","اذكر شيئًا يجب عليك فعله في العمل كل يوم.","I have to answer a lot of emails every day."],
["Ask someone politely to send you something.","اطلب من شخص بأدب أن يرسل لك شيئًا.","Could you send me the form by email, please?"]],
t:[
["Make it polite with \"Could you…?\"","اجعلها مهذبة باستخدام Could you.","Tell me the interest rate.","Could you tell me the interest rate, please?"],
["Make it polite with \"I'd like to\".","اجعلها مهذبة باستخدام I'd like to.","I want to ask about a loan.","I'd like to ask about a loan."],
["Use \"have to\".","استخدم have to.","A down payment is necessary.","You have to pay a down payment."]],
q:[
["How can I help you today?","كيف أساعدك اليوم؟","I'd like to ask about opening an account.","I'd like to · Could you"],
["What documents do I need to bring?","ما المستندات التي أحتاج إلى إحضارها؟","You need to bring your ID and a salary certificate.","you need to · you have to"],
["Can I do this online?","هل أستطيع عمل هذا عبر الإنترنت؟","Yes, you can, but you have to sign the form at the branch.","you can · you have to"]],
rp:["You are the bank officer. A customer asks about a loan. Be polite and clear.","أنت موظف البنك. عميل يسأل عن قرض. كن مهذبًا وواضحًا.",
["Good morning. I'd like to ask about a home loan.","Of course. Could you tell me how much you would like to borrow?","About two million pounds. What do I need?","You have to bring your ID, a salary certificate, and bank statements."]],
talk:["Explain to a customer, step by step, how to apply for a service at your bank or company. Be polite.","اشرح لعميل خطوة بخطوة كيف يتقدم بطلب خدمة في بنكك أو شركتك. كن مهذبًا.","first · you have to · you need to · you can · could you",
"Thank you for coming in today. First, you have to fill in the application form. You also need to bring your ID, a salary certificate, and bank statements for six months. Then we check the documents, and it usually takes two to three weeks. You can choose the term that suits you. Could you give me your email, please? I'll send you all the details today."]},

d21:{p:[
["Say one rule at your workplace with \"must\".","اذكر قاعدة في مكان عملك باستخدام must.","We must wear our ID cards at all times."],
["Say one thing you mustn't do at work.","اذكر شيئًا يُمنع عليك فعله في العمل.","We mustn't share customer information."],
["Say one thing you don't have to do on your day off.","اذكر شيئًا لا يلزمك فعله في يوم إجازتك.","I don't have to wake up early on Fridays."]],
t:[
["Change it to a prohibition with \"mustn't\".","حوّلها إلى منع باستخدام mustn't.","Don't use your phone here.","You mustn't use your phone here."],
["Say it is not necessary.","قل إن ذلك ليس ضروريًّا.","You must wear a tie on Thursdays.","You don't have to wear a tie on Thursdays."],
["Make a question with \"have to\".","كوّن سؤالًا باستخدام have to.","We sign in every morning.","Do we have to sign in every morning?"]],
q:[
["Do I have to wear a suit to the meeting?","هل يجب أن أرتدي بدلة في الاجتماع؟","No, you don't have to, but you must look professional.","you don't have to · you must"],
["Can I take these files home?","هل أستطيع أخذ هذه الملفات إلى البيت؟","No, I'm sorry. You mustn't take documents out of the building.","you mustn't"],
["What must new staff do in the first week?","ماذا يجب على الموظفين الجدد في الأسبوع الأول؟","They must finish the safety training.","they must · they have to"]],
rp:["A new employee asks you about the rules.","موظف جديد يسألك عن القواعد.",
["It's my first day. What time do we have to be here?","You must arrive by eight thirty and sign in.","And what about phones?","You mustn't use your phone in the cash area."]],
talk:["Explain the most important rules of your workplace to a new colleague: what is necessary, what is forbidden, and what is optional.","اشرح أهم قواعد مكان عملك لزميل جديد: ما هو ضروري، وما هو ممنوع، وما هو اختياري.","you must · you mustn't · you have to · you don't have to",
"Welcome to the team. There are a few important rules. You must wear your ID card at all times, and you must arrive by eight thirty. You mustn't share your password with anyone, and you mustn't leave customer files on your desk. You have to finish the safety training this month. You don't have to wear a tie on Thursdays. If there is a problem, you must report it immediately."]},

d22:{p:[
["Say who you call most often and why.","قل من تتصل به أكثر ولماذا.","I call my wife every afternoon to ask her about the kids."],
["Say something you sent to someone this week.","اذكر شيئًا أرسلته إلى شخص هذا الأسبوع.","I sent my manager a report, and he thanked me for it."],
["Ask someone to wait for you.","اطلب من شخص أن ينتظرك.","Could you wait for me for five minutes, please?"]],
t:[
["Replace the names with pronouns.","استبدل الأسماء بضمائر.","I sent the contract to Mr. Sami.","I sent it to him."],
["Replace the names with pronouns.","استبدل الأسماء بضمائر.","Please tell Mona and Ali.","Please tell them."],
["Replace the names with pronouns.","استبدل الأسماء بضمائر.","Can you help my colleague and me?","Can you help us?"]],
q:[
["Can I take a message for him?","هل أترك له رسالة؟","Yes, please. Could you ask him to call me back?","ask him to · tell him"],
["Did you get my email?","هل وصلك بريدي الإلكتروني؟","Yes, I got it this morning. Thank you for sending it.","I got it · I didn't get it"],
["Could you spell your name for me?","هل يمكنك أن تتهجّى لي اسمك؟","Of course. It's M-A-H-M-O-U-D.","Of course · It's"]],
rp:["You call a company, but the person you want is not available.","تتصل بشركة، لكن الشخص الذي تريده غير متاح.",
["Good morning, Delta Company. How can I help you?","Good morning. Could I speak to Ms. Hala, please?","I'm sorry, she's in a meeting. Can I take a message for her?","Yes, please. Could you ask her to call me back before five?"]],
talk:["Leave a clear voicemail message: say who you are, who the message is for, why you are calling, and how to reach you.","اترك رسالة صوتية واضحة: قل من أنت، ولمن الرسالة، ولماذا تتصل، وكيف يمكن الوصول إليك.","this is · it's for · please tell him / her · call me back",
"Hello, this is Mahmoud from the bank. This message is for Mr. Sami. I'm calling about the contract. I sent it to him this morning, and I'd like him to check it. Could you ask him to call me back before five? I'll give you my number again. Please tell him it's important. Thank you for your help."]},

d23:{p:[
["Say how well you speak English now.","قل ما مدى إجادتك للإنجليزية الآن.","I speak English quite well, but I still speak slowly."],
["Say how you usually drive.","قل كيف تقود عادةً.","I usually drive carefully, especially at night."],
["Say how you deal with customers or colleagues.","قل كيف تتعامل مع العملاء أو الزملاء.","I always try to listen patiently and answer politely."]],
t:[
["Use the adverb.","استخدم الظرف.","He is a careful driver.","He drives carefully."],
["Use the adverb.","استخدم الظرف.","She is a good speaker.","She speaks well."],
["Use the adverb.","استخدم الظرف.","They are hard workers.","They work hard."]],
q:[
["How do you want me to fill in this form?","كيف تريدني أن أملأ هذه الاستمارة؟","Please fill it in carefully and write clearly.","carefully · clearly"],
["I didn't understand. Could you say that again?","لم أفهم. هل يمكنك إعادة ما قلت؟","Of course. I'll speak more slowly.","more slowly · more clearly"],
["How well do you know this system?","ما مدى معرفتك بهذا النظام؟","I know it pretty well. I use it every day.","pretty well · very well · not very well"]],
rp:["Your manager gives you feedback.","مديرك يعطيك ملاحظاته على أدائك.",
["You handled that customer very well.","Thank you. I tried to listen patiently.","You also explained the product clearly. How did you learn that?","I practiced a lot, and I always prepare carefully."]],
talk:["Describe how a good employee works. Use at least six adverbs.","صِف كيف يعمل الموظف الجيد. استخدم ستة ظروف على الأقل.","well · hard · carefully · quickly · politely · clearly · patiently",
"A good employee works hard and learns fast. She reads every document carefully and answers emails quickly. She speaks clearly, and she always deals with customers politely. When there is a problem, she listens patiently and stays calm. She works well with the team, and she finishes her projects successfully."]},

d24:{p:[
["Say what you will do if you finish work early today.","قل ماذا ستفعل إذا أنهيت عملك مبكرًا اليوم.","If I finish early today, I'll go to the gym."],
["Say what you will do if it is hot this weekend.","قل ماذا ستفعل إذا كان الجو حارًّا في العطلة.","If it's hot this weekend, we'll stay at home."],
["Say what will happen if you practice English every day.","قل ماذا سيحدث إذا تدربت على الإنجليزية كل يوم.","If I practice every day, my English will improve."]],
t:[
["Join the two with \"if\".","اربط الجملتين باستخدام if.","You leave now. You catch the train.","If you leave now, you'll catch the train."],
["Make the result negative.","اجعل النتيجة منفية.","If the price goes up, we'll buy it.","If the price goes up, we won't buy it."],
["Start with the result.","ابدأ بالنتيجة.","If I need help, I'll call you.","I'll call you if I need help."]],
q:[
["What will you do if you miss your flight?","ماذا ستفعل إذا فاتتك الرحلة؟","If I miss it, I'll take the next one.","If I … , I'll …"],
["What happens if I pay early?","ماذا يحدث إذا دفعت مبكرًا؟","If you pay early, you'll get a discount.","If you … , you'll …"],
["What if the customer doesn't answer?","ماذا لو لم يرد العميل؟","If he doesn't answer, I'll send him an email.","If he doesn't … , I'll …"]],
rp:["A customer asks about an offer. Explain the conditions.","عميل يسأل عن عرض. اشرح له الشروط.",
["I saw your offer online. How does it work?","If you apply this month, you'll get a lower fee.","And if I apply online?","If you apply online, it'll be faster."]],
talk:["Talk about your plans for next weekend with different conditions (weather, work, family).","تحدّث عن خططك للعطلة القادمة مع شروط مختلفة (الطقس، العمل، الأسرة).","if · I'll · we'll · won't · when",
"I have a few plans for next weekend. If the weather is nice, we'll go to the park. If it rains, we'll stay at home and watch a movie. If I finish my work early on Thursday, I'll visit my parents. If my brother comes, we'll have lunch together. And if I have time, I'll study English for an hour."]},

d25:{p:[
["Say a country or city you have visited.","اذكر بلدًا أو مدينة زرتها.","I've been to Luxor twice."],
["Say something you have never done.","اذكر شيئًا لم تفعله قط.","I've never ridden a horse."],
["Say a food you have tried and liked.","اذكر طعامًا جرّبته وأعجبك.","I've tried Indian food, and I loved it."]],
t:[
["Make it negative with \"never\".","حوّلها إلى النفي باستخدام never.","I've seen the pyramids at night.","I've never seen the pyramids at night."],
["Make a question with \"ever\".","كوّن سؤالًا باستخدام ever.","You've flown in a balloon.","Have you ever flown in a balloon?"],
["Change \"I\" to \"my wife\".","غيّر I إلى my wife.","I've visited five countries.","My wife has visited five countries."]],
q:[
["Have you ever worked abroad?","هل عملت في الخارج من قبل؟","No, I haven't, but I've worked with international teams.","Yes, I have · No, I haven't"],
["Have you ever missed a flight?","هل فاتتك رحلة طيران من قبل؟","No, I've never missed a flight in my life.","I've never"],
["What's the best place you've ever visited?","ما أفضل مكان زرته في حياتك؟","The best place I've ever visited is Aswan.","the best … I've ever"]],
rp:["Small talk with a visitor from abroad.","حديث ودّي مع زائر من الخارج.",
["Have you ever been to Europe?","Yes, I have. I've been to Italy once.","Lovely. Have you ever tried real Italian pizza?","Yes, I have. It's the best pizza I've ever eaten."]],
talk:["Talk about your life experiences: places you have been, things you have tried, and things you have never done.","تحدّث عن تجاربك في الحياة: أماكن زرتها، وأشياء جرّبتها، وأشياء لم تفعلها قط.","I've been · I've never · I've tried · once · twice · many times",
"I've traveled a lot in Egypt. I've been to Luxor twice, and I've visited Alexandria many times. I've never been to Asia, but I'd love to go. I've tried sushi once, but I've never tried Thai food. I've met people from all over the world at work. The best trip I've ever taken was to Aswan with my family."]},

d26:{p:[
["Say something you have just finished.","اذكر شيئًا أنهيته للتو.","I've just finished a meeting."],
["Say something you have already done today.","اذكر شيئًا فعلته بالفعل اليوم.","I've already answered all my emails."],
["Say something you haven't done yet today.","اذكر شيئًا لم تفعله بعد اليوم.","I haven't had lunch yet."]],
t:[
["Add \"just\".","أضف just.","The client has signed the contract.","The client has just signed the contract."],
["Make it negative with \"yet\".","حوّلها إلى النفي باستخدام yet.","She has replied.","She hasn't replied yet."],
["Make a question with \"yet\".","كوّن سؤالًا باستخدام yet.","The meeting has started.","Has the meeting started yet?"]],
q:[
["Have you sent the report yet?","هل أرسلت التقرير بعد؟","Yes, I've already sent it.","I've already · Not yet"],
["Has the manager arrived?","هل وصل المدير؟","Yes, she's just arrived.","she's just · not yet"],
["Is everything ready for the launch?","هل كل شيء جاهز للإطلاق؟","Almost. We haven't chosen a date yet.","we've already · we haven't … yet"]],
rp:["Your manager asks for a quick update.","مديرك يطلب تحديثًا سريعًا.",
["Where are we with the monthly report?","I've just finished it.","Great. Have you sent it to the head office yet?","Not yet, but I've already checked the numbers."]],
talk:["Give your team a short progress update: what you have just done, what you have already finished, and what you haven't done yet.","قدّم لفريقك تحديثًا قصيرًا: ما أنجزته للتو، وما انتهيت منه بالفعل، وما لم تفعله بعد.","I've just · we've already · we haven't … yet · so far",
"Good morning, everyone. Here is a quick update. I've just finished the monthly report, and I've already sent it to the manager. She hasn't replied yet. The client has just signed the contract, so we've already reached our target this month. We haven't chosen a date for the launch yet. I'll let you know as soon as we decide."]},

l3:{p:[
["Say how long you have worked in your field.","قل منذ متى تعمل في مجالك.","I've worked in banking for more than fifteen years."],
["Say when you started your first job.","قل متى بدأت أول وظيفة لك.","I started my first job in two thousand and nine."],
["Say one thing you have learned recently.","اذكر شيئًا تعلمته مؤخرًا.","I've recently learned how to build reports in Excel."]],
t:[
["Add \"last year\" and change the tense.","أضف last year وغيّر الزمن.","I've led a digital project.","I led a digital project last year."],
["Remove the time and change the tense.","احذف الزمن وغيّر صيغة الفعل.","I managed a team in 2020.","I've managed a team."],
["Make a question with \"ever\".","كوّن سؤالًا باستخدام ever.","You led a large project.","Have you ever led a large project?"]],
q:[
["Tell me about your experience.","حدّثني عن خبرتك.","I've worked in banking for fifteen years. I started in sales, and now I manage products.","I've worked · I started · now I"],
["What is your biggest achievement?","ما أكبر إنجاز لك؟","Last year, my team increased sales by thirty percent.","last year · increased · by"],
["Why do you want this role?","لماذا تريد هذا المنصب؟","I'm looking for more responsibility, and I like your company's culture.","I'm looking for · I like"]],
rp:["You are in a job interview.","أنت في مقابلة عمل.",
["Thank you for coming. Have you ever managed a team?","Yes, I have. I've managed teams of up to twenty people.","Good. When did you start in management?","I started in two thousand and fifteen, at my previous bank."]],
talk:["Answer \"Tell me about yourself\" as in a job interview: your experience, one achievement with a date, and what you are looking for.","أجب عن Tell me about yourself كما في مقابلة عمل: خبرتك، وإنجاز واحد بتاريخه، وما تبحث عنه.","I've worked · I started · last year · I've always · I'm looking for",
"Thank you for inviting me. I've worked in banking for more than fifteen years. I started my career in sales in two thousand and nine, and I've managed teams of up to twenty people. Last year, my team increased sales by thirty percent. I've always enjoyed working with customers, and my biggest strength is solving problems under pressure. Now I'm looking for a role with more responsibility."]},

d28:{p:[
["Say why you are learning English, using \"because\".","قل لماذا تتعلم الإنجليزية مستخدمًا because.","I'm learning English because I need it for my career."],
["Say something that was hard but that you did, using \"but\".","اذكر شيئًا كان صعبًا لكنك فعلته، مستخدمًا but.","The exam was difficult, but I passed it."],
["Say what you did first and then this morning.","قل ماذا فعلت أولًا ثم بعد ذلك هذا الصباح.","First, I had breakfast. Then I drove to work."]],
t:[
["Join the two with \"because\".","اربط الجملتين باستخدام because.","I changed my job. I wanted a new challenge.","I changed my job because I wanted a new challenge."],
["Join the two with \"so\".","اربط الجملتين باستخدام so.","I was worried. I called a friend.","I was worried, so I called a friend."],
["Join the two with \"but\".","اربط الجملتين باستخدام but.","The questions were difficult. I answered them calmly.","The questions were difficult, but I answered them calmly."]],
q:[
["Why did you choose your current job?","لماذا اخترت وظيفتك الحالية؟","I chose it because I like working with people.","because · so"],
["What happened after the interview?","ماذا حدث بعد المقابلة؟","After that, I waited for a week. Finally, they called me.","after that · then · finally"],
["Was it an easy decision?","هل كان قرارًا سهلًا؟","No, it wasn't easy, but it was the right decision.","but · although"]],
rp:["A friend asks how you got your job.","صديق يسألك كيف حصلت على وظيفتك.",
["How did you get your job at the bank?","First, I sent my CV. Then they called me for an interview.","Were you nervous?","Yes, I was nervous, but I prepared well, so it went fine."]],
talk:["Tell a short story about an important change in your life. Use at least five linking words.","احكِ قصة قصيرة عن تغيير مهم في حياتك. استخدم خمس أدوات ربط على الأقل.","first · then · after that · because · so · but · finally",
"Last year I decided to change my job because I wanted a new challenge. First, I updated my CV and sent it to three banks. I waited for two weeks, but nobody called me. I was worried, so I asked a friend for advice. Then one morning my phone rang. After that, I had an interview. Finally, they offered me the job, and I accepted immediately."]},

d29:{p:[
["Say one goal for this year, using \"want to\".","اذكر هدفًا لهذا العام مستخدمًا want to.","I want to reach level B1 this year."],
["Say something you enjoy doing after work.","اذكر شيئًا تستمتع بفعله بعد العمل.","I enjoy walking in the evening."],
["Say a habit you have stopped or want to stop.","اذكر عادة توقفت عنها أو تريد التوقف عنها.","I've stopped drinking coffee at night."]],
t:[
["Complete it with the right form of the verb in brackets.","أكملها بالصيغة الصحيحة للفعل بين القوسين.","I enjoy (listen) to podcasts.","I enjoy listening to podcasts."],
["Complete it with the right form of the verb in brackets.","أكملها بالصيغة الصحيحة للفعل بين القوسين.","I've decided (study) every day.","I've decided to study every day."],
["Complete it with the right form of the verb in brackets.","أكملها بالصيغة الصحيحة للفعل بين القوسين.","I keep (make) the same mistakes.","I keep making the same mistakes."]],
q:[
["What do you hope to do next year?","ماذا تأمل أن تفعل العام القادم؟","I hope to get a promotion and improve my English.","I hope to · I plan to"],
["What do you enjoy most about your job?","ما أكثر ما تستمتع به في عملك؟","I enjoy solving problems and working with my team.","I enjoy …ing"],
["Do you mind working late sometimes?","هل تمانع العمل لوقت متأخر أحيانًا؟","No, I don't mind working late when it's necessary.","I don't mind …ing"]],
rp:["Your manager asks about your development plan.","مديرك يسألك عن خطة تطويرك.",
["What would you like to improve this year?","I want to improve my English, and I need to practice presenting.","Good. How do you plan to do that?","I've decided to study every day, and I hope to take an exam in June."]],
talk:["Talk about your goals: what you want to do, what you need to do to get there, what you enjoy, and what you have stopped doing.","تحدّث عن أهدافك: ما تريد فعله، وما تحتاج إلى فعله للوصول إليه، وما تستمتع به، وما توقفت عن فعله.","I want to · I need to · I've decided to · I enjoy …ing · I've stopped …ing",
"I want to improve my English this year, so I need to practice speaking every day. I've decided to study for an hour a day. I enjoy listening to podcasts in the car, and I'm trying to learn ten new words a day. I've stopped watching TV in the evening. I hope to reach level B1 by December, and I plan to take an exam next year."]},

d30:{p:[
["Say what you do, where you live, and who you live with.","قل ما عملك، وأين تسكن، ومع من تعيش.","I'm a product manager, and I live in Giza with my family."],
["Compare your English one month ago with now.","قارن لغتك الإنجليزية قبل شهر بلغتك الآن.","A month ago, I couldn't speak without stopping. Now I'm speaking more confidently."],
["Say your next step.","قل ما خطوتك التالية.","Next month, I'm going to start the B1 level."]],
t:[
["Change it to the past.","حوّلها إلى الماضي.","I practice for two hours every day.","I practiced for two hours every day."],
